    - The significance of these finds for understanding the emergence of 
Mycenaean civilization and early European states.
    - Institutional sponsors and brief biographies of Davis and Stocker.

---

These sources collectively provide:

- Primary, detailed treatment of the Ring of Nestor (Evans 1925 monograph; 
ResearchGate article on authenticity).
- Museum and catalog data confirming location and inventory (National 
Archaeological Museum references; CMS citations via UChicago article).
- Scholarly debates and iconographic analyses (Cambridge “Fakes and Dubitanda”; 
“Traces of Places”; Davis’s work on gold rings).
- Contextual information from Pylos excavations (Griffin Warrior-related 
sources) and non‑technical narratives (The Past, The History Blog, lecture 
announcement).

