"source_id": "20260628152251782676_93905c8c", "text": "The ResearchGate-hosted 
scholarly article titled \"The Pseudo-Minoan Nestor Ring and Its Egyptian 
Iconography\" examines the Ring of Nestor with emphasis on its classification as
\"pseudo-Minoan\" and its strong Egyptian iconographic components. It cites 
Evans’s earlier publication of the ring and undertakes detailed comparisons 
between specific motifs on the ring and Egyptian reliefs or objects. The article
discusses the ring’s cultural attribution and dating, questioning whether it is 
an authentic Late Bronze Age artifact or a later creation inspired by Egyptian 
and Minoan styles, and contributes to debates about the degree of Egyptian 
influence on Aegean art and the possibility of later imitations or forgeries."},
