"20260628152251706798_280e6a9f", "text": "The Past magazine article on the 
Griffin Warrior tomb at Pylos surveys the rich grave goods and compares them 
with other notable Mycenaean finds. In discussing gold signet rings from the 
region it notes that similar high-status rings were previously known, mentioning
the famous Ring of Nestor as one of these and identifying it as the only other 
such ring from the area besides a particular ring from Tholos IV. The article 
states that the Ring of Nestor was purchased by Arthur Evans, linking it to his 
role in excavating Knossos and in collecting Mycenaean artifacts, and uses it as
a comparator for the artistic and cultural significance of the Griffin Warrior 
material."}, {"id": "20260628152251881299_e9f601b3", "type": "Document", 
"source_id": "20260628152251680187_d268dd55", "text": "The Heidelberg 
scroll-view entry for Evans’s work provides navigational structure and confirms 
the contents: a title page, a first section on the sepulchral treasure of gold 
signet-rings and bead-seals from Thisbê, a second section on a glimpse into the 
Minoan after-world, and plates I–V. It identifies the digitized item as historic
scholarly literature in the Heidelberg University Library collections and 
indicates that the detailed descriptions of the treasure and individual rings, 
including the one designated as the ring of Nestor, together with their 
illustrations, are accessible through these pages."}, {"id": 
