scholarly article hosted on Academia.edu focuses on the iconography of the 
\"ring of Nestor.\" It analyzes the engraved scenes on the ring, situating them 
within ongoing debates on Aegean forgeries and authenticity. The study compares 
the ring’s imagery with other Minoan and Mycenaean motifs, revisits Evans’s 
interpretations and later scholarship, and reassesses the cultural attribution, 
chronological placement, and possibly the authenticity of the ring and its 
iconography within the broader corpus of Aegean art."}, {"id": 
