Minoan glyptic in a Cambridge University Press monograph on Aegean Bronze Age 
art and archaeology. It includes a brief catalog-style entry for a gold signet 
ring known as the 'Ring of Nestor' from Kakovatos in Messenia, providing its 
length (3.27 cm), material (gold), cultural period (Late Minoan IB–II, 
approximately 1530–1400 BCE), current holding institution (Ashmolean Museum, 
Oxford), and inventory number (1938.1130). The entry situates the ring within 
the corpus of Minoan glyptic and uses standard chronological terminology."}, 
