[AIMessage → tool] create_analysis({'text': 'Available evidence indicates that 
the name "Ring of Nestor" has been applied to at least two related but not 
identical contexts: Evans\x19s monograph presents a gold signet ring from a 
sepulchral treasure near Thisb\x17 in Boeotia as the ring of Nestor, tied to a 
glimpse into the Minoan after-world, whereas later catalog and glyptic 
literature locates a gold signet ring known as the Ring of Nestor in Kakovatos, 
