{"query": {"id": "20260628152024465885_acb469c8", "handle": "q1", "text": "“Ring
of Nestor” gold ring archaeological find -site:en.wikipedia.org", "importance": 
"core"}, "items": [{"id": "20260628152253134034_5d102d93", "type": "Evidence", 
"text": "Evans’s monograph is titled \"The ring of Nestor. A glimpse into the 
Minoan after-world and a sepulchral treasure of gold signet-rings and bead-seals
from Thisbê, Boeotia\" and is divided into Part I \"Sepulchral treasure of gold 
signet-rings and bead-seals from Thisbê, Boeotia\" (pp. 1–42) and Part II \"A 
glimpse into the Minoan after-world\" (pp. 43–75).", "source_ids": 
["20260628152251657830_e85ded99"], "citations": [9]}, {"id": 
"20260628152253196069_c63bfe00", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The Heidelberg 
metadata lists keywords including \"Nestor; Ring; Minoische Kultur; Thísvi; 
Europe; Greece; Kakóvatos,\" indicating thematic focus on a ring associated with
Nestor, Minoan culture, and the Boeotian site of Thísvi/Thisbê.", "source_ids": 
["20260628152251657830_e85ded99"], "citations": [9]}, {"id": 
"20260628152253252658_72af3f23", "type": "Evidence", "text": "Evans describes 
the treasure as consisting of multiple gold signet rings and bead-seals found in
connection with a Mycenaean rock-cut tomb near Thisbê in Boeotia.", 
"source_ids": ["20260628152251657830_e85ded99"], "citations": [9]}, {"id": 
"20260628152253311219_8da3c892", "type": "Evidence", "text": "Evans singles out 
one particular gold signet ring from the treasure, assigns it the name \"the 
ring of Nestor,\" and discusses its beaded hoop and elaborate engraved scenes as
central to his interpretation of the Minoan after-world.", "source_ids": 
["20260628152251657830_e85ded99"], "citations": [9]}, {"id": 
"20260628152253374163_3b556ecc", "type": "Evidence", "text": "In Part II, Evans 
uses motifs and compositions on the Nestor ring and related rings to propose 
representations of an afterworld or funerary journey, comparing them with seal 
imagery from Crete, Mycenaean Greece, and Egyptian motifs.", "source_ids": 
["20260628152251657830_e85ded99"], "citations": [9]}, {"id": 
"20260628152253428218_5728e783", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The Heidelberg 
scroll-view lists the contents of Evans’s work as \"Titelblatt\"; \"1–42 I. 
Sepulchral treasure of gold signet-rings and bead-seals from Thisbê, Boeotia\"; 
\"43–75 II. A glimpse into the Minoan after-world\"; and \"Tafel I – V\" 
(plates).", "source_ids": ["20260628152251680187_d268dd55"], "citations": [10]},
{"id": "20260628152253482713_1f989ea3", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The 
scroll-view interface identifies the work as digitized historic literature 
within Heidelberg University Library’s digital collections and notes that 
detailed discussion and illustrations of the gold rings and bead-seals, 
including the ring designated by Evans as the \"ring of Nestor,\" are 
available.", "source_ids": ["20260628152251680187_d268dd55"], "citations": 
[10]}, {"id": "20260628152253538785_a5098c1d", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The 
Griffin Warrior article states that a particular gold signet ring from Tholos IV
is one of the notable Mycenaean gold rings and that \"the only other from this 
area was the famous Ring of Nestor – purchased by Arthur Evans, famous for his 
work at Knossos.\"", "source_ids": ["20260628152251706798_280e6a9f"], 
"citations": [11]}, {"id": "20260628152253594441_c8d01819", "type": "Evidence", 
"text": "Evans’s 1936 lecture notes a lion-spearing scene in \"the later group 
at Thisbê\" and compares the spear-shaft with signet rings from Mycenae and 
other Boeotian gold objects.", "source_ids": ["20260628152251729228_5d864f18"], 
"citations": [12]}, {"id": "20260628152253651861_8146ba49", "type": "Evidence", 
"text": "The lecture mentions a gold bead obtained in 1910 from a Boeotian 
peasant and later acquired for the Ashmolean Museum, which Evans compares 
stylistically with the Thisbê series.", "source_ids": 
["20260628152251729228_5d864f18"], "citations": [12]}, {"id": 
"20260628152253713347_b1d2d294", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The Academia.edu 
article is described in the search results as presenting \"some observations on 
the iconography of the 'ring of nestor'\" and situating the ring within debates 
about Aegean forgeries and authenticity.", "source_ids": 
["20260628152124716216_d7950336"], "citations": [3]}, {"id": 
"20260628152253778793_ded4b508", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The ResearchGate 
listing gives the title \"The Pseudo-Minoan Nestor Ring and Its Egyptian 
Iconography\" and cites Evans’s earlier article \"The 'Ring of Nestor': A 
Glimpse into the Minoan After-World\" from the Journal of Hellenic Studies.", 
"source_ids": ["20260628152251782676_93905c8c"], "citations": [13]}, {"id": 
"20260628152253840511_3b939a76", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The ResearchGate 
article’s focus on \"Egyptian Iconography\" indicates that the author undertakes
detailed comparison between motifs on the Nestor ring and Egyptian visual 
material to assess its stylistic origins and authenticity.", "source_ids": 
["20260628152251782676_93905c8c"], "citations": [13]}, {"id": 
"20260628152253903403_52e905ec", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The Cambridge Core
epilogue section heading includes the phrase \"Beaded gold hoop resembling that 
of ‘Ring of Nestor’; Parallel arrangement of designs—three successive scenes\" 
in describing a royal signet ring.", "source_ids": 
["20260628152251811261_9fe900ea"], "citations": [14]}, {"id": 
"20260628152253955675_bdc6a2f4", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The epilogue uses 
the Ring of Nestor as a benchmark to describe the royal signet ring’s beaded 
gold hoop and the layout of its three successive engraved scenes.", 
"source_ids": ["20260628152251811261_9fe900ea"], "citations": [14]}, {"id": 
"20260628152439758117_7ede2aac", "type": "Claim", "text": "The \"Ring of 
Nestor\" is a gold signet ring with a beaded hoop and elaborate engraved scenes,
originally part of a sepulchral treasure of gold signet rings and bead‑seals 
discovered in association with a Mycenaean rock‑cut tomb near Thisbê (Thísvi) in
Boeotia, Greece, and designated and interpreted as the \"ring of Nestor\" by 
Arthur Evans.", "source_ids": ["20260628152251657830_e85ded99"], "citations": 
[9]}, {"id": "20260628152439951130_9b4fbfd9", "type": "Claim", "text": "Arthur 
Evans published a monograph titled \"The ring of Nestor. A glimpse into the 
Minoan after‑world and a sepulchral treasure of gold signet‑rings and bead‑seals
from Thisbê, Boeotia\", structured in two parts that describe the Thisbê 
treasure and use the Ring of Nestor’s imagery to propose interpretations of a 
Minoan after‑world, with illustrated plates of the rings.", "source_ids": 
["20260628152251657830_e85ded99", "20260628152251680187_d268dd55"], "citations":
[9, 10]}, {"id": "20260628152440097008_f1aaa7da", "type": "Claim", "text": "The 
Ring of Nestor has been used as a comparative benchmark for other Aegean royal 
or Mycenaean gold signet rings, particularly with regard to its beaded gold hoop
and arrangement of engraved designs in three successive scenes.", "source_ids": 
["20260628152251706798_280e6a9f", "20260628152251811261_9fe900ea"], "citations":
[11, 14]}, {"id": "20260628152440256839_fef5ddbd", "type": "Claim", "text": 
"Later scholarship has questioned the cultural attribution and authenticity of 
the Ring of Nestor, describing it as \"pseudo‑Minoan\" and emphasizing Egyptian 
iconography in its engraved scenes, and situating it within broader debates 
about Aegean forgeries and Late Bronze Age stylistic influences.", "source_ids":
["20260628152124716216_d7950336", "20260628152251782676_93905c8c"], "citations":
[3, 13]}, {"id": "20260628152440398318_4a6ea1af", "type": "Claim", "text": 
"Arthur Evans interpreted the Ring of Nestor’s imagery by associating it with 
the Homeric figure Nestor and by using its motifs, alongside related rings, to 
propose visual representations of a Minoan after‑world or funerary journey, 
drawing comparisons with Cretan, Mycenaean, and Egyptian seal imagery.", 
"source_ids": ["20260628152251657830_e85ded99"], "citations": [9]}], "offset": 
0, "limit": 20, "total": 21, "next_offset": 20}
