Siegel.", "source_ids": ["20260628152124716216_d7950336", 
"20260628152124746007_b5bc2226", "20260628152124788632_ce48f530"], "citations": 
[3, 4, 5]}, {"id": "20260628152439570572_5c30b592", "type": "Claim", "text": 
"Recent research by Vlachopoulos argues that the Ring of Nestor is authentic, in
contrast to earlier scholarship that questioned or denied its authenticity.", 
"source_ids": ["20260628152124654716_343e1a7d", "20260628152124746007_b5bc2226",
"20260628152124788632_ce48f530"], "citations": [1, 4, 5]}, {"id": 
"20260628153003072480_82c9a1fc", "type": "Claim", "text": "Scholarly opinion on 
the authenticity of the Ring of Nestor has been divided, with some classifying 
it as a doubtful gem or ‘gemma dubitanda’ and others arguing, in more recent 
research, that the ring is authentic.", "source_ids": 
["20260628152124654716_343e1a7d", "20260628152124746007_b5bc2226", 
"20260628152124788632_ce48f530", "20260628152841748020_95f45291", 
"20260628152841807143_6101ab94"], "citations": [1, 4, 5, 28, 30]}, {"id": 
"20260628153140970289_76484a79", "type": "Claim", "text": "The Ring of Nestor is
a gold signet ring from Kakovatos in Messenia, now housed in the Ashmolean 
Museum in Oxford under inventory number 1938.1130.", "source_ids": 
["20260628152124687708_7516438c"], "citations": [2]}, {"id": 
"20260628153141112897_87186450", "type": "Claim", "text": "The Ring of Nestor is
described in catalog and scholarly sources as a gold signet ring with overall 
dimensions around 3.3 cm in length and approximately 3.29 × 2.18 cm for its oval
bezel, making it among the largest Aegean signet rings (ranked about fifth in 
size).", "source_ids": ["20260628152124654716_343e1a7d", 
"20260628152124687708_7516438c"], "citations": [1, 2]}, {"id": 
"20260628153141231680_579ee8ce", "type": "Claim", "text": "Current scholarship 
dates the Ring of Nestor from Kakovatos to the Late Minoan IB–II period, 
approximately 1530–1400 BCE.", "source_ids": ["20260628152124687708_7516438c"], 
"citations": [2]}, {"id": "20260628153141303584_29e57846", "type": "Claim", 
"text": "The engraved iconography of the Ring of Nestor has been the focus of 
dedicated scholarly analysis, particularly in relation to Aegean forgeries and 
debates over authenticity.", "source_ids": ["20260628152124716216_d7950336"], 
"citations": [3]}, {"id": "20260628153141562841_c928f9b5", "type": "Claim", 
"text": "The Ring of Nestor is included in the Corpus der minoischen und 
mykenischen Siegel as catalog item no. 277, and has been a key case study in 
discussions of Aegean iconography and authenticity.", "source_ids": 
["20260628152124716216_d7950336", "20260628152124746007_b5bc2226"], "citations":
[3, 4]}], "offset": 0, "limit": 20, "total": 19, "next_offset": null}
[tools:5c466b60-2619-2e00-0d8b-aba6ab21001e] [get_report_evidence result] 
{"query": {"id": "20260628153250024085_56b9f76d", "handle": "q3.4", "text": 
"\"Ring of Nestor\" provenance Evans Davis rock-cut chamber tomb near Thisbe 
Boeotia vs Mycenaean Pylos signet ring Benedante Alexandria jewelry blog 
cross-check primary excavation reports museum catalogues acquisition records 
1900-2026", "importance": "core"}, "items": [{"id": 
"20260628153403375836_3764f864", "type": "Evidence", "text": "目录题名为：“The 
ring of Nestor; a glimpse into the Minoan after-world, and a sepulchral treasure
of gold signet-rings and bead-seals from Thisbê, Boeotia”，作者标注为“Sir Arthur
J. Evans”，出版信息显示地点伦敦、年份1925。", "source_ids": 
["20260628152407087140_b91ef2dd"], "citations": [16]}, {"id": 
"20260628153403438167_6fc1ee3c", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"埃文斯专著封面印有完整题名：“The ring of Nestor. A glimpse into the Minoan 
after-world and a sepulchral treasure of gold signet-rings and bead-seals from 
Thisbê, Boeotia”，下方注明作者“Sir Arthur J. Evans”和出版地“London 
1925”。目录中列出章节“I. Sepulchral treasure of gold signet-rings and bead-seals
from Thisbê, Boeotia; 43–75”。", "source_ids": 
["20260628153402781836_4405eddf"], "citations": [39]}, {"id": 
"20260628153403512555_806a44f2", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"论文摘要指出：“Here new technical observations are presented which serve to 
support the authenticity of the Ring of Nestor. In 1995 the ring was once again 
placed on display 
...”，表明作者通过技术分析支持戒指为真品，并提到其在1995年重新展出。", 
"source_ids": ["20260628152841748020_95f45291"], "citations": [28]}, {"id": 
"20260628153403579000_68b68867", "type": "Evidence", "text": "《SOME 
OBSERVATIONS ON THE ICONOGRAPHY OF THE “RING OF 
NESTOR”》的说明指出该文旨在分析“the iconography surrounding the 'Ring of Nestor'
in the context of Aegean forgeries and authenticity 
debates”，显示作者将戒指图像置入爱琴伪作与真伪讨论框架。", "source_ids": 
["20260628152124716216_d7950336"], "citations": [3]}, {"id": 
"20260628153403648840_ca43acd4", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"在关于格里芬战士墓的论文中，作者写道：“Both the Ring of Nestor and the Ring of 
Minos have bands strikingly similar ... For the Ring of Nestor, see Evans 1925, 
p. 47, fig. 
42.”，以戒环形制相似为论点，并直接引用埃文斯1925年第47页图42作为“Ring of 
Nestor”的参考。", "source_ids": ["20260628153402847685_711d3e54"], "citations": 
[40]}, {"id": "20260628153429272939_663ba7f1", "type": "Claim", "text": "Arthur 
J. Evans consistently described the so‑called 'Ring of Nestor' and its 
associated gold signet-rings and bead-seals as part of a sepulchral treasure 
from a rock-cut tomb near Thisbê in Boeotia, and modern Aegean and Pylos 
scholarship continues to cite his 1925 publication as the standard reference for
this ring.", "source_ids": ["20260628152407087140_b91ef2dd", 
"20260628153402781836_4405eddf", "20260628153402847685_711d3e54"], "citations": 
[16, 39, 40]}, {"id": "20260628153429506209_1ba0fb21", "type": "Claim", "text": 
"Contemporary scholarship treats the 'Ring of Nestor' as an important piece of 
Aegean iconography whose authenticity has been debated; recent technical 
analyses have been presented in support of its authenticity, and by 1995 the 
ring was once again placed on public display in a museum collection.", 
"source_ids": ["20260628152124716216_d7950336", 
"20260628152841748020_95f45291"], "citations": [3, 28]}, {"id": 
"20260628153429668444_b060835f", "type": "Claim", "text": "The gold band of the 
'Ring of Nestor' has been noted in recent work on the Pylos Griffin Warrior tomb
as being morphologically very similar to the bands of the 'Ring of Minos' and to
gold rings from the Griffin Warrior grave, and Evans 1925 (p. 47, fig. 42) is 
cited as the standard illustration for the 'Ring of Nestor' in that comparative 
context.", "source_ids": ["20260628153402847685_711d3e54"], "citations": [40]}],
"offset": 0, "limit": 20, "total": 8, "next_offset": null}
